{
  "manufacturer": "Janitza",
  "manufacturer_slug": "janitza",
  "model": "UMG 96-S2 energy analyser (serial Modbus)",
  "model_slug": "umg-96-s2",
  "short_model": "UMG 96-S2",
  "aliases": [
    "UMG96-S2",
    "UMG 96 S2",
    "UMG96S2",
    "Janitza UMG96-S2"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power meter (energy analyser)",
  "applies_to": "UMG 96-S2 energy analyser, per address list 2.062.026.1.b (10/2019).",
  "summary": "The UMG 96-S2 is an energy analyser with a serial Modbus slave port (baud and framing set by parameters 1 and 2). Values are big-endian 32-bit floats that include the CT/VT ratios. This map covers the 19000-19120 'frequently required readings' block (volts, amps, power, PF, frequency, energy, THD), total power factor, the bus and transformer parameters, the digital output source and the reset commands.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are printed as the protocol address and sent unchanged: 19000 is requested as 19000. The parameter list starts at address 0 (device address), which only fits 0-based numbering. In a 1-based or Modicon tool enter 19001 / 419001."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Energy Analyser UMG 96-S2 - Modbus-address list and Formulary",
    "doc_number": "2.062.026.1.b",
    "revision_date": "2019-10",
    "url": "https://www.janitza.com/files/download/manuals/current/UMG96-S2/janitza-mal-umg96s2-en.pdf",
    "pages": "Functions p. 4; transfer parameters, byte order, number formats p. 5; frequently required readings pp. 12-13; parameters p. 14; measured values p. 15"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Byte order: the list says its addresses return data big-endian (high byte first, high word in the lower register = ABCD). Adding 32768 to an address returns the same value little-endian; that mirror block is not listed.",
    "Unlike other Janitza lists, 19044-19048 are printed as 'power factor' (not CosPhi), 19068 is the consumed L1-L3 total, and the rotation field 19052 is an int (signed 32-bit) rather than a float.",
    "Transfer parameters (p. 5): 9600, 19200 or 38400 baud, 8 data bits; the page names odd/even parity and 1 or 2 stop bits, while parameter 2 also offers stop-bit-only framing. The list gives no defaults, so defaults are left blank.",
    "Parameter 0 is printed with a range of 0-255 and a footnote mark whose text is not on the page; use 1-247 for a normal Modbus slave address.",
    "Left out: display, averaging-time and threshold parameters, the pulse valence at 102 (range given but no unit beyond 'e.g. imp/kWh'), tariff assignment bits, mean/min/max blocks, tariff energy and the double-type energy copies.",
    "The address list names no physical interface (RS-485) or framing mode (RTU); RTU is assumed from the serial baud/parity parameters. Confirm in the device user manual."
  ],
